---
import Article from '../../layouts/Article.astro';
import CompareTable from '../../components/compare/CompareTable.astro';
import Cite from '../../components/compare/Cite.astro';
import MoveCode from '../../components/compare/MoveCode.astro';
import Related from '../../components/compare/Related.astro';
import Sources from '../../components/compare/Sources.astro';
import { S } from '../../components/compare/siar';
import { RIVALS, CHECKED, citeHtml } from '../../data/rivals';

const r = RIVALS.postiz;
const x = r.facts;
const c = r.cells;

const faq = [
  { q: 'What is the Postiz API rate limit?', a: 'Postiz documents 90 create-post requests an hour (100 on its cloud), on every plan. One request can carry several posts.' + citeHtml(x.rate) },
  { q: 'Can I self-host Siar?', a: 'No. Siar is hosted only. If you must run the software on your own server, Postiz is the better choice.' },
];
---
<Article
  metaTitle="Postiz alternative: a hosted social media API | Siar"
  h1="Postiz alternative: a hosted API for products that publish for their customers"
  description={`Postiz caps channels and create-post requests per hour. Siar is a hosted, unified social media API with no channel cap, signed webhooks and a comments API.`}
  kicker="Compare"
  updated={CHECKED}
  crumbs={[{ name: 'Compare', href: '/compare' }, { name: 'Postiz alternative', href: '/compare/postiz' }]}
  lead={`Postiz is an open-source scheduler, capped by connected channels and by about 100 create-post requests an hour. Siar, a unified social media API, is hosted, has no channel cap, signs its webhooks and lets you read and answer comments over the API. If you want to own the code or run it on your own server, Postiz is the better choice.`}
  actions="quickstart"
  faq={faq}
>
  <CompareTable rival={r} />

  <h2 id="where-postiz-wins">Where Postiz is the better choice</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>You want open source or self-hosting.</strong> {c.entry!.value.split('. ').slice(1).join('. ')} (<Cite f={c.entry!} />). Siar is hosted only.</li>
    <li><strong>You need many networks.</strong> {c.networks!.value} (<Cite f={c.networks!} />). On Siar: {S.tiktok} {S.pinterest} {S.linkedin}</li>
    <li><strong>You post a lot.</strong> {x.unlimited.value} (<Cite f={x.unlimited} />). Siar caps posts per month: {S.starterPosts}, {S.proPosts} and {S.businessPosts} by plan.</li>
    <li><strong>You want a hosted MCP server.</strong> Postiz runs one (<Cite f={c.mcp!} />). Siar's is not hosted: {S.tooling}</li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="rate-limit">Postiz API rate limit</h2>
  <p>{x.rate.value} (<Cite f={x.rate} />). One request can carry several posts, so compare requests, not posts. Siar's limits are per API key, in windows of a second, ten seconds and a minute; the <a href="/docs/rate-limits">rate limits guide</a> lists them.</p>

  <h2 id="what-siar-adds">What Siar adds for a product that publishes for its customers</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>No channel cap.</strong> {S.unitLine} Postiz counts every connected account as a channel (<Cite f={c.unit!} />).</li>
    <li><strong>Comments over the API.</strong> Read and answer comments where the network allows. {x.comments.value} (<Cite f={x.comments} />).</li>
    <li><strong>Signed webhooks.</strong> Siar signs each webhook and retries it for about 45 hours. Postiz's webhook {c.webhooks!.value.charAt(0).toLowerCase() + c.webhooks!.value.slice(1)} (<Cite f={c.webhooks!} />).</li>
    <li><strong>A branded connect link</strong> for your customers, on every plan.</li>
    <li><strong>A free start with no card.</strong> {S.freeStart}. {x.noFree.value} (<Cite f={x.noFree} />).</li>
    <li><strong>Nothing to host.</strong> Siar holds its own network apps for the networks open today: {S.openList}.</li>
  </ul>

  <MoveCode>
    <p>Postiz integrations map to Siar social accounts, and a Postiz customer group maps to a Siar brand. In the API a brand is a team. Replace invite links with a Siar connect link per brand; each customer connects again. A Postiz post with several integrations becomes one Siar post with a payload per network.</p>
  </MoveCode>

  <Related />
  <Sources rivals={[r]} />
</Article>
